WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:05.220
These LEDS are the beginning
of the Internet of Light.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.560
They can sense light,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.600
emit light,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.240
and collect energy all in one

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.180
The key is a thin film of
spherical semiconductors

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.040
called quantum dots
attached to nanorods

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.500
The asymmetrical design allows them
to perform multiple functions

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.320
The nanorod gathers electrons

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.280
while a shell around the dot
gathers positive charges

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.580
The quantum dot takes both to generate light

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:34.219
Switching the voltage makes the process reverse

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:35.619
The dot collects light

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:37.719
and feeds an electron to the rod

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:40.259
and a positive charge to the shell

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.430
Ordinary spherical quantum
dots can’t do this

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.870
They switch between collecting
light and emitting it

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.250
faster than the human eye can see

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.700
so it looks like they're
emitting light continuously

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.260
In the future, screens made
from this technology

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.440
could “see” without need of a camera

00:00:57.449 --> 00:00:59.409
TV screens or electronic billboards

00:00:59.409 --> 00:01:02.509
could respond to touchless gestures,

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.650
phones and tablets could
adjust to dappled light,

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:10.970
and any two screens could communicate 
with each other using “LiFi”

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.710
Since these LEDs can also collect energy,

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.000
your phone could charge from
whatever light hits the screen

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.320
Having multi-function instead of single-function
devices makes fabrication easier

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.460
So far, these experimental LEDs
can only produce a single color

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.200
and a small array of pixels

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.450
But improving this tech could open up a new
way for us to interact with our devices

